ADAPTIVE INTELLIGENCE THEORY

FINAL SYNTHESIS


THE CORE MODEL


An intelligent system is a recursive process:

Reality
  ↓
Representation
  ↓
Compression
  ↓
Prediction
  ↓
Action
  ↓
Reality Change
  ↓
Feedback
  ↺


The purpose of intelligence is not merely to optimize.

It is to improve the loop itself.


--------------------------------------------------


THE THREE FUNDAMENTAL QUESTIONS


1. REPRESENTATION

Can the system build an accurate and useful model of reality?


R = f(Environment)


Better representations create larger reachable futures.


--------------------------------------------------


2. REACHABILITY

What futures become possible because of the system?


Ω(S) = reachable future space


Capability is:

ΔΩ > 0


But intelligence expands both opportunity and risk.


--------------------------------------------------


3. STABILITY

Can the system correct itself faster than it changes the world?


Alignment condition:

Correction capacity ≥ Capability growth


A system remains safe when adaptation keeps pace with influence.


--------------------------------------------------


THE UNIFYING PRINCIPLE


All major concepts are different views of the same process:


Resolution Horizon:
    limits of what can currently be known


Representation Elasticity:
    ability to update internal models


Interface-Induced Computational Geometry:
    tools changing what computation is possible


Causal Mass / CRM:
    how much future space depends on a system


Causal Permeability:
    ability to absorb corrective information


CGET:
    balance between generative expansion and stabilizing constraints


Alignment Spine:
    keeping capability connected to correction


--------------------------------------------------


FINAL STATEMENT


Adaptive Intelligence Theory studies how systems increase their ability to model, transform, and create reality while preserving the feedback mechanisms required to remain aligned.


The goal is not maximum intelligence.

The goal is:

maximum adaptive capability
with preserved correction.
